<title>HUNGARY: Soproni swings to profits in Q1.</title>
<headline>Soproni swings to profits in Q1.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three-month period ending March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>					  Jan-March 1997   Jan-March 1996</p>
<p>    Group operating profit	  10.6 profit vs    139.3 loss</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit	     9.8 profit vs    163.0 loss</p>
<p>    Group net sales		2,895.9	  vs  2,894.7</p>
<p>    Group other revenue	     10.8	  vs     15.4</p>
<p>    Material expenditures	2,109.1	  vs  2,453.3</p>
<p>    Personnel expenditures	 251.5	  vs    190.5</p>
<p>    Depreciation		     152.5	  vs    146.3</p>
<p>    Other costs			330.7	  vs    168.0</p>
<p>    Other expenditures	     102.9	  vs     72.1</p>
<p>    Net financial income	     3.4 loss   vs     15.5 loss</p>
<p>	Financial revenue	     16.1	  vs	3.7</p>
<p>	Financial expenditure	 19.5	  vs     19.2</p>
<p>    Net extraordinary income	 2.6 profit vs	8.2 loss</p>
<p>	Extraordinary revenue	 14.7	  vs	2.8</p>
<p>	Extraordinary expenditure   12.1	  vs     11.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Soproni Sorgyar Rt is a brewery, majority owned by Austria's Brau Union AG. The figures are consolidated.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
